THE MEASUREMENT BRACKETS THAT THRESHOLD RATHER THAN CLEARING IT.
  defensible range: n_eff ~6.4 (correlogram, rho floored) to ~26
  (30-degree blocks), against a crossover at 7.9. The asserted 20 sits
  inside it and on the ADOPTING side.
  Ruled OUT by the measurement: the full-spread sigma 45.88 (n_eff = 1),
  which was the only one of the five original candidates that rejected A,
  and Kish's 3408, which assumes an independence the correlogram refutes.
  So the range narrows from 15x asserted to ~4x measured -- but it lands
  ACROSS the threshold, not clear of it.

