STILL NOT MEASURED BY ANY OF THIS, and both push sigma UP:
 * model REPRESENTATION error -- a one-box deep ocean against a field
   spanning -234 to -87 permil. R/likelihood.R records it as deliberately
   zero. It is Marcus' open question, not settled here.
 * UNSAMPLED VOLUME -- part 5 has no bathymetry denominator.
A measured n_eff therefore sets a CEILING on the term's weight, not the
weight itself. Do not read the largest n_eff as licence for the smallest
sigma.


